 "build_recommendation": "Do not build learned dead-end reflexes (negative: <=0.4 calls/task, subtracts from U11). Build the learned outcome detector only as a replacement for the hand-written signature lists where Adage labels outcomes (adage-learn outcome.rs env_signature/executed_tests, the replay's ENV_SIG): a Drain template dictionary (~14k templates, ~1.3 MB) + a logistic regression over hashed templates, taught by exit status on non-piped calls, ~12 ms/output in Python. Expected value: better labels (AUC 0.96 vs 0.92; 0.85 vs 0.57 on piped failures) for any learner, $0 direct saving; its value is only what a downstream lever built on it earns. Ship the pre-emptive U11 rewrite first (+1.6 calls, +3.5% of $).",
 "so_what": "If shipped as reflexes: about +0.2 calls/task [-0.07, +0.42], +0.2% of $ [-0.3, +0.8] on Haiku held-out (split), <0.5% of $ in any protocol; confidence it survives a live A/B as a positive effect: low. As a labeller it is a better instrument, not a lever; ceiling for any dead-end lever is ~10-13% of $."
}